(function(payload){if(typeof applySerialChapterPayload==="function")applySerialChapterPayload(payload);else (window.SERIAL_CHAPTER_QUEUE||(window.SERIAL_CHAPTER_QUEUE=[])).push(payload);})({"id":"serial-cultivation-21","book":"mountain-ledger","cn":["堡门前，孩子抓着一小袋[[cereal|谷物]]，罗清用[[scissors|剪刀]]剪开伤者腿上的湿布，露出旧[[scar|伤疤]]。沈砚试图找关税与封河的[[connexion|关联]]，守关人却说留下盐才是[[reasonable|合理的]]办法。许庭认为这最[[effective|有效]]，指着[[overhead|头顶的]]税旗要大家顺从。旗绳下的木梁有一道如[[vein|叶脉]]的裂纹，守卫的[[tone|语气]]也忽然紧张，因为梁正在下沉。一匹马在门边[[graze|吃草]]，咬出草丛里埋的断桩。新湿泥不是雨水，是坝后漏出的河水。","车队有另绕山路的[[option|选择]]，许庭却[[reluctant|不愿意]]绕，怕损货。罗清指向洪水的[[victim|受害者]]，说人不是他的[[asset|财产]]。货箱里香料的[[fragrance|芳香]]盖住湿粮酸味，车轮的[[gear|传动装置]]已有泥沙。抢过将塌的门洞是[[insane|荒唐的]]主意；新添的盐税也是旧费之外的[[addition|加收款]]。一个替许庭赶羊的人对他近乎[[passion|热烈的]]讨好，递来[[lamb|小羊]]作关礼，守卫却也看见门梁，没敢接。沈砚请他先让无车的人走干路，自己留下量水。","上游村的[[cooperative|合作社]]正把难民送到[[fort|堡垒]]外，正值汛期的[[eve|前夕]]。最[[vulnerable|脆弱的]]孩子没有地方过夜，[[civil|文职的]]关吏只数粮袋的[[figure|数字]]。罗清把衣包作[[pillow|枕头]]，安顿一个昏睡的老人，不使他靠在危险梁下。许庭还数着[[commodity|货物]]，终于闻到河水带来的[[scent|气味]]。沈砚请一名[[professional|专业的]]堤工说水势，要求他给出[[explicit|明确的]]避让距离。堤工名叫季禾，袖里露出熔炉灼出的旧斑，说梁坏只是表面，河岸正向堡里移动。","季禾认为见人不救是[[sin|罪过]]，却不要求谁献命。援手必须[[voluntary|自愿]]，他画一张旧坝[[sketch|略图]]，指出河水为何会[[perplex|使人困惑]]地从背后出来：一条废弃[[trench|沟]]被新土封住。远处[[lightning|闪电]]亮起，墙面的[[plaster|灰泥]]已浮出湿泡。守卫原说难民有义务[[bound|受约束]]留在堡外，听见梁里的[[roar|轰鸣]]后，终于抬起横杆。赶羊人低声说下月要[[marry|成婚]]，不想死在这趟货上；许庭没有回应，伸手替他推住倾斜的车。","沈砚不得不[[reassess|重新评估]]路线。季禾的[[boss|老板]]曾负责修坝，图页[[margin|边缘]]还留着料钱。他说新坝填料可能夹[[toxic|有毒的]]矿渣，需留样再判断。沈砚把自己的[[thinking|想法]]向车队说明：不能只因山村缺盐，就同意关吏[[arbitrary|专断的]]扣货。湿麻袋不断[[absorb|吸收]]污水，干净水比盐更[[invaluable|宝贵]]。孩子的杯子已满到[[brim|杯沿]]，季禾让他倒掉这杯河边水，递去车队带来的清水。罗清记录来源，免得日后把所有发病都怪给逃难的人。","他们拆下一扇无用的税栏，把车上的粮抬过梁外干地。放人没有让货也自动通行，关吏仍扣了两车盐。许庭留下货号，第一次愿意和合作社共同封箱，因为漏水会把他的货也毁掉。沈砚手疼，无法搬重物，便数过关人数，防止老人被漏下。季禾说旧堤的料册在上一处渡仓，若能证明改岸，关吏就不能把灾情只说成天雨。今晚须沿山路走，明早要从渡仓把那份册子拿出来；堡后的河已开始咬住第二根桩。"],"en":["At the fort, a child held [[cereal|cereal]]. Luo used [[scissors|scissors]] to uncover a leg’s old [[scar|scar]]. Shen sought the [[connexion|connexion]] between taxes and closure. The guard called surrendering salt [[reasonable|reasonable]]. Xu thought compliance [[effective|effective]], pointing to the flag [[overhead|overhead]]. A [[vein|vein]]-like crack crossed its beam; the guard’s [[tone|tone]] tightened as it sank. A horse began to [[graze|graze]] and exposed a broken buried pile. Water, not rain, had soaked the new mud.","They had the [[option|option]] of a mountain detour. Xu was [[reluctant|reluctant]], fearing damaged cargo. Luo said a flood [[victim|victim]] was not his [[asset|asset]]. Spice [[fragrance|fragrance]] hid sour grain, and mud filled the wheel’s [[gear|gear]]. Rushing the failing gateway was [[insane|insane]]; the salt levy was an unexplained [[addition|addition]]. A shepherd with flattering [[passion|passion]] offered a [[lamb|lamb]] as a gate gift. The guard now feared the beam too. Shen asked him to let pedestrians use dry ground while he measured water.","An upstream [[cooperative|cooperative]] brought refugees outside the [[fort|fort]] on the [[eve|eve]] of the flood season. [[vulnerable|Vulnerable]] children lacked beds; a [[civil|civil]] official counted only the cargo [[figure|figure]]. Luo made a [[pillow|pillow]] from clothes for an elderly sleeper. Xu counted [[commodity|commodity]] boxes until the water’s [[scent|scent]] reached him. A [[professional|professional]] embankment worker gave [[explicit|explicit]] safe distances. His name was Ji He; furnace scars marked his sleeve. The beam was only a symptom: the bank was moving into the fort.","Ji considered ignoring people a [[sin|sin]], but required [[voluntary|voluntary]] help, not sacrifice. His [[sketch|sketch]] showed why water would [[perplex|perplex]] watchers by coming from behind: fresh earth blocked an old [[trench|trench]]. [[lightning|Lightning]] revealed wet bubbles in [[plaster|plaster]]. Guards had said refugees were [[bound|bound]] to remain outside; a beam’s [[roar|roar]] made them lift the barrier. The shepherd said he would [[marry|marry]] next month and did not want to die here. Xu silently supported his tilted wagon.","Shen had to [[reassess|reassess]] the route. Ji’s former [[boss|boss]] had repaired the dam, with costs still in the map’s [[margin|margin]]. The new fill might contain [[toxic|toxic]] slag, pending sampling. Shen explained his [[thinking|thinking]]: village need could not justify [[arbitrary|arbitrary]] seizure. Sacks continued to [[absorb|absorb]] dirty water; clean drinking water was [[invaluable|invaluable]]. Ji replaced the child’s river cup, filled to its [[brim|brim]], with carried water. Luo recorded its source rather than blaming refugees for every later illness.","They dismantled an unused tax barrier and carried grain across dry ground. Passage for people did not free the two detained salt carts. Xu listed cargo numbers and agreed to shared sealing because leakage threatened his goods too. Shen could not lift, but counted people so the elder was not forgotten. Ji said dam material records lay at the next ferry store. Proof of altered banks would challenge the rain-only excuse. They would take the mountain path tonight and retrieve that ledger tomorrow. The river had begun eating a second pile."]});
